rsa-private-prime-only: store only the RSA prime in the sensitive area (RSA_PRIVATE_PRIME_ONLY)

Classification: profile setting.

RSA_PRIVATE_SIZE = MAX_RSA_KEY_BYTES / 2 is a vendor option (Part 2,
TPM2B_PRIVATE_KEY_RSA note). tpm-rs stores only the prime in the sensitive
area of every RSA key, so the reference does so also for keys with fixedTPM
parents (where it would otherwise keep the full CRT values). Adds the
RSA_PRIVATE_PRIME_ONLY switch to TpmProfile_Misc.h and uses it in
MarshalSensitive().

diff --git a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Misc.h b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Misc.h
--- a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Misc.h
+++ b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Misc.h
@@ -34,6 +34,10 @@
 #define NUM_STATIC_PCR             16
 #define MAX_ALG_LIST_SIZE          64
 #define PRIMARY_SEED_SIZE          32
+// tpm-rs differential testing: vendor choice RSA_PRIVATE_SIZE =
+// MAX_RSA_KEY_BYTES / 2 (Part 2, TPM2B_PRIVATE_KEY_RSA note): the sensitive
+// area of an RSA key holds only the prime, also under fixedTPM parents.
+#define RSA_PRIVATE_PRIME_ONLY     YES
 #define CONTEXT_ENCRYPT_ALGORITHM  AES
 #define NV_CLOCK_UPDATE_INTERVAL   22
 #define NUM_POLICY_PCR             1
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/Object_spt.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/Object_spt.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/Object_spt.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/Object_spt.c
@@ -1038,7 +1038,11 @@ static UINT16 MarshalSensitive(
         // If the parent isn't fixedTPM, then truncate the sensitive data to be
         // the size of the prime. Otherwise, leave it at the current size which
         // is the full CRT size.
-        if(parent == NULL
+        // tpm-rs differential testing: RSA_PRIVATE_PRIME_ONLY selects the
+        // vendor-specific RSA_PRIVATE_SIZE = MAX_RSA_KEY_BYTES / 2 option
+        // (Part 2, TPM2B_PRIVATE_KEY_RSA note), i.e. only the prime is stored
+        // even for keys with fixedTPM parents (as tpm-rs does).
+        if(RSA_PRIVATE_PRIME_ONLY || parent == NULL
            || !IS_ATTRIBUTE(
                parent->publicArea.objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, fixedTPM))
             sensitive->sensitive.rsa.t.size /= 5;
